From 202606fc22554f966f2927c12840699bb15ab8c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:15:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] unixbridge: Calls from a Windows program into a Unix library
 of its own.

A program (or a DLL it loads) that comes with a Unix library for the
machine it runs on opens it by its Unix path (unixbridge_open) and calls
its unixbridge_entry(code, args) (unixbridge_call) with a pointer into
its own memory; for a 32-bit program the pointer and what it points at
are 32-bit ones.
